<LST>Note 3:  Pumping stability is tested by pumping<MET> 475 ml</MET><ENG> 1 pint</ENG> of diluted material at<MET> 25 deg C</MET><ENG> 77 deg F</ENG>,through a<MET> 6 mm</MET><ENG> 1/4 inch</ENG> gear pump 
operation 1,750 rpm for 10 minutes with no significant separation or coagulation.</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>The bituminous base residue must contain not less than 20 percent uintaite or gilsonite, and must not contain any tall oil pitch or coal tar material.   
This must be stated in the <SUB>Manufacturer's Certificate of Compliance</SUB> for <SUB>bituminous material</SUB>.  The material must be compatible with asphaltic concrete, 
and have a 5-year minimum proven performance record at airports with similar climatic conditions. Curing time, under recommended application conditions, 
must not exceed eight hours.</TXT><BRK/>
